  "rationale": "F. The CRM caps an external order list at 20 rows when no date filter is given (_EXTERNAL_ORDERS_LIST_LIMIT_CAP, orders.py:22), nothing in the envelope reports truncation, and the probe asks about EVERY candidate in ONE flat date-ordered page. Measured on exec 13590613: one busy customer filled all 20 rows, so five other candidates were never reached and would each have rendered a confident '- no delivery' on evidence that was never gathered. All 20 rows here belong to A CRAFT IDEA, which is exactly that shape. Mirrors dym-annotate's _PAGE_SATURATION: a saturated page withholds the annotation entirely and can never invent one. Note it withholds it from A CRAFT IDEA too, even though that one IS proven to have deliveries - a page half of whose lines are measured and half guessed is the asymmetry the suppress-all rule exists to avoid."
